text: ['({T}: Add {B}.)', '({T}: Add {G}.)', '({T}: Add {R}.)', '({T}: Add {U}.)', '({T}: Add {W}.)', 'All creatures get -1/-1 until end of turn.', "All lands become 2/2 creatures until end of turn. They're still lands.", 'As Brass Herald enters the battlefield, choose a creature type.\\nWhen Brass Herald enters the battlefield, reveal the top four cards of your library. Put all creature cards of the chosen type revealed this way into your hand and the rest on the bottom of your library in any order.\\nCreatures of the chosen type get +1/+1.', 'As Shifting Sky enters the battlefield, choose a color.\\nAll nonland permanents are the chosen color.', 'As Story Circle enters the battlefield, choose a color.\\n{W}: The next time a source of your choice of the chosen color would deal damage to you this turn, prevent that damage.', "At the beginning of each player's draw step, if Howling Mine is untapped, that player draws an additional card.", "At the beginning of each player's draw step, that player puts the cards in their hand on the bottom of their library in any order, then draws that many cards.", "At the beginning of each player's upkeep, Karma deals damage to that player equal to the number of Swamps they control.", 'At the beginning of your upkeep, you draw a card and you lose 1 life.', "Beast of Burden's power and toughness are each equal to the number of creatures on the battlefield.", 'Blaze deals X damage to any target.', 'Change the target of target spell with a single target.', 'Change the text of target permanent by replacing all instances of one color word with another or one basic land type with another. (For example, you may change "nonblack creature" to "nongreen creature" or "forestwalk" to "islandwalk." This effect lasts indefinitely.)', 'Choose a color. Target player reveals their hand and discards all cards of that color.', 'Choose one —\\n• Target player gains 3 life.\\n• Prevent the next 3 damage that would be dealt to any target this turn.', 'Coastal Tower enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {W} or {U}.', 'Counter target creature spell.', 'Counter target instant spell.', 'Counter target spell unless its controller pays {3}.', 'Counter target spell. Untap up to four lands.', "Creature spells can't be countered.", "Creatures don't untap during their controllers' untap steps.\\nWhenever a creature enters the battlefield, untap all creatures.", "Creatures with power greater than the number of cards in your hand can't attack.", 'Creatures you control get +0/+5 until end of turn.', 'Creatures you control get +1/+1.', "Defender (This creature can't attack.)", "Defender (This creature can't attack.)\\nFirst strike", "Defender (This creature can't attack.)\\nFlying", "Defender (This creature can't attack.)\\nFlying\\nSunweb can't block creatures with power 2 or less.", "Defender (This creature can't attack.)\\n{1}{B}: Regenerate Carrion Wall.", "Defender (This creature can't attack.)\\n{T}: Add {G}.", "Defender, flying (This creature can't attack, and it can block creatures with flying.)", 'Defender\\nWhen Cinder Wall blocks, destroy it at end of combat.', 'Destroy all Islands.', 'Destroy all Plains.', "Destroy all creatures you don't control. They can't be regenerated.", "Destroy all creatures. They can't be regenerated.", 'Destroy target artifact or enchantment.', 'Destroy target artifact or land.', 'Destroy target artifact, enchantment, or land.', 'Destroy target artifact.', 'Destroy target attacking creature. You gain life equal to its power.', 'Destroy target creature with flying.', 'Destroy target enchantment.', "Destroy target green creature. It can't be regenerated.\\nDraw a card.", 'Destroy target land.', "Destroy target nonblack creature. It can't be regenerated.", "Destroy target nonblack creature. It can't be regenerated. You gain life equal to its toughness.", 'Destroy target tapped creature.', "Destroy target white creature. It can't be regenerated.\\nDraw a card.", 'Discard a land card: Seismic Assault deals 2 damage to any target.', 'Draw a card for each creature you control.', 'Draw three cards.', 'Draw two cards, then discard a card.', 'Each creature gets +1/+1 for each other creature on the battlefield that shares at least one creature type with it. (For example, if two Goblin Warriors and a Goblin Shaman are on the battlefield, each gets +2/+2.)', "Each spell costs {3} more to cast except during its controller's turn.", 'Elfhame Palace enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {G} or {W}.', "Enchant Swamp\\nWhen enchanted land becomes tapped, destroy it.\\nWhen Spreading Algae is put into a graveyard from the battlefield, return Spreading Algae to its owner's hand.", 'Enchant artifact\\nYou control enchanted artifact.', "Enchant creature (Target a creature as you cast this. This card enters the battlefield attached to that creature.)\\nEnchanted creature doesn't untap during its controller's untap step.", "Enchant creature (Target a creature as you cast this. This card enters the battlefield attached to that creature.)\\nEnchanted creature has fear. (It can't be blocked except by artifact creatures and/or black creatures.)", 'Enchant creature (Target a creature as you cast this. This card enters the battlefield attached to that creature.)\\nEnchanted creature has first strike. (It deals combat damage before creatures without first strike.)', 'Enchant creature (Target a creature as you cast this. This card enters the battlefield attached to that creature.)\\nWhenever enchanted creature deals damage, you gain that much life.', "Enchant creature (Target a creature as you cast this. This card enters the battlefield attached to that creature.)\\n{G}: Regenerate enchanted creature. (The next time that creature would be destroyed this turn, it isn't. Instead tap it, remove all damage from it, and remove it from combat.)", 'Enchant creature\\nAll creatures able to block enchanted creature do so.', "Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature can't attack or block.", "Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature can't be blocked except by Walls.", 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +1/+1 for each Forest you control.', 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +1/+2.', 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +2/+1.', 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature has flying.', 'Enchant creature\\nWhenever enchanted creature deals damage to an opponent, you may draw a card.', "Enchant land\\nEnchanted land is a 5/6 green Treefolk creature that's still a land.", 'Enchant land\\nWhenever enchanted land is tapped for mana, its controller adds an additional one mana of any color.', 'Enchant permanent\\nYou control enchanted permanent.', 'Exile all nontoken permanents. Starting with you, each player chooses one of the exiled cards and puts it onto the battlefield tapped under their control. Repeat this process until all cards exiled this way have been chosen.', "Fear (This creature can't be blocked except by artifact creatures and/or black creatures.)", 'First strike', 'First strike (This creature deals combat damage before creatures without first strike.)', "First strike\\nWhen Nekrataal enters the battlefield, destroy target nonartifact, nonblack creature. That creature can't be regenerated.", 'Flying', "Flying (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)", "Flying (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)\\nFirst strike (This creature deals combat damage before creatures without first strike.)", "Flying (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)\\nNightmare's power and toughness are each equal to the number of Swamps you control.", "Flying (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)\\nSacrifice Spiketail Hatchling: Counter target spell unless its controller pays {1}.", "Flying (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)\\nWhen Aven Cloudchaser enters the battlefield, destroy target enchantment.", "Flying (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)\\nWhen Aven Fisher dies, you may draw a card.", "Flying (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)\\nWhenever Blinding Angel deals combat damage to a player, that player skips their next combat phase.", "Flying (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)\\nWhenever Thieving Magpie deals damage to an opponent, draw a card.", "Flying (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)\\n{1}{U}: Return Fleeting Image to its owner's hand.", "Flying (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)\\n{R}: Shivan Dragon gets +1/+0 until end of turn.", "Flying (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)\\n{W}: Aven Flock gets +0/+1 until end of turn.", 'Flying, vigilance', "Flying\\nGoblin Glider can't block.", "Flying\\nMenace (This creature can't be blocked except by two or more creatures.)\\nTwo-Headed Dragon can block an additional creature each combat.\\n{1}{R}: Two-Headed Dragon gets +2/+0 until end of turn.", 'Flying\\nSacrifice a creature: Fallen Angel gets +2/+1 until end of turn.', 'Flying\\nWhen Angel of Mercy enters the battlefield, you gain 3 life.', 'Flying\\nWhen Sage Owl enters the battlefield, look at the top four cards of your library, then put them back in any order.', 'Flying\\nWhen Vampiric Spirit enters the battlefield, you lose 4 life.', 'Flying\\nWhenever Abyssal Specter deals damage to a player, that player discards a card.', 'Flying\\n{T}: Add one mana of any color.', 'Flying\\n{T}: Target attacking or blocking creature gets +1/+1 until end of turn.', "Forestwalk (This creature can't be blocked as long as defending player controls a Forest.)", "Goblin Raider can't block.", 'Guerrilla Tactics deals 2 damage to any target.\\nWhen a spell or ability an opponent controls causes you to discard Guerrilla Tactics, Guerrilla Tactics deals 4 damage to any target.', 'Hammer of Bogardan deals 3 damage to any target.\\n{2}{R}{R}{R}: Return Hammer of Bogardan from your graveyard to your hand. Activate only during your upkeep.', 'Haste (This creature can attack and {T} as soon as it comes under your control.)', "Haste (This creature can attack and {T} as soon as it comes under your control.)\\nAt the beginning of the end step, return Viashino Sandstalker to its owner's hand. (Return it only if it's on the battlefield.)", 'Haste\\nWhen Lava Hounds enters the battlefield, it deals 4 damage to you.', "Hulking Cyclops can't block.", 'If a source would deal damage to a permanent or player, it deals double that damage to that permanent or player instead.', 'If a source would deal damage to you, prevent 1 of that damage.', 'If target opponent has more cards in hand than you, draw cards equal to the difference.', 'If you control a creature, damage that would reduce your life total to less than 1 reduces it to 1 instead.', 'If you have 3 or less life, this spell costs {6} less to cast.\\nFlying\\nAvatar of Hope can block any number of creatures.', 'Inferno deals 6 damage to each creature and each player.', "Islands don't untap during their controllers' untap steps.", 'Lava Axe deals 5 damage to target player or planeswalker.', "Lhurgoyf's power is equal to the number of creature cards in all graveyards and its toughness is equal to that number plus 1.", 'Lightning Blast deals 4 damage to any target.', 'Look at the top five cards of your library, then put them back in any order.', "Maro's power and toughness are each equal to the number of cards in your hand.", "Mountainwalk (This creature can't be blocked as long as defending player controls a Mountain.)", 'Nonbasic lands are Mountains.', "Ogre Taskmaster can't block.", "Okk can't attack unless a creature with greater power also attacks.\\nOkk can't block unless a creature with greater power also blocks.", "Other Elf creatures get +1/+1 and have forestwalk. (They can't be blocked as long as defending player controls a Forest.)", 'Other Goblins get +1/+1 and have mountainwalk.', 'Other Zombie creatures get +1/+1.\\n{1}{B}, {T}: Return target Zombie card from your graveyard to your hand.', 'Pay 2 life: Regenerate Deepwood Ghoul.', "Phantom Warrior can't be blocked.", "Phyrexian Colossus doesn't untap during your untap step.\\nPay 8 life: Untap Phyrexian Colossus.\\nPhyrexian Colossus can't be blocked except by three or more creatures.", "Players play with their hands revealed.\\nIf a player would draw a card, they reveal it instead. Then any other player may pay 2 life. If a player does, put that card into its owner's graveyard. Otherwise, that player draws a card.", 'Prevent all combat damage that would be dealt this turn.', 'Prevent all damage that would be dealt this turn to up to two target creatures.', "Put two target lands on top of their owners' libraries.", 'Pyroclasm deals 2 damage to each creature.', 'Pyrotechnics deals 4 damage divided as you choose among any number of targets.', 'Rain of Blades deals 1 damage to each attacking creature.', 'Reach (This creature can block creatures with flying.)', 'Reach (This creature can block creatures with flying.)\\nSacrifice a land: Spitting Spider deals 1 damage to each creature with flying.', "Return all creatures to their owners' hands.", "Return all green permanents to their owners' hands.", 'Return target creature card from your graveyard to the battlefield.', 'Return target creature card from your graveyard to your hand.', "Return target creature to its owner's hand.", 'Return target green card from your graveyard to your hand.', "Return target permanent to its owner's hand.", 'Sacrifice Shock Troops: It deals 2 damage to any target.', 'Sacrifice a land: Coastal Hornclaw gains flying until end of turn.', 'Salt Marsh enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {U} or {B}.', "Sea Monster can't attack unless defending player controls an Island.", "Search target opponent's library for a creature card and put that card onto the battlefield under your control. Then that player shuffles.", 'Search your library for a basic land card, put that card onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', 'Search your library for a blue instant card, reveal that card, put it into your hand, then shuffle.', 'Search your library for a card, put that card into your hand, then shuffle.', 'Searing Wind deals 10 damage to any target.', 'Shivan Oasis enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {R} or {G}.', 'Shock deals 2 damage to any target.', 'Sizzle deals 3 damage to each opponent.', "Sneaky Homunculus can't block or be blocked by creatures with power 2 or greater.", "Spineless Thug can't block.", 'Star Compass enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add one mana of any color that a basic land you control could produce.', "Sudden Impact deals damage to target player equal to the number of cards in that player's hand.", "Swampwalk (This creature can't be blocked as long as defending player controls a Swamp.)", "Swarm of Rats's power is equal to the number of Rats you control.", 'Tap an untapped creature you control: Llanowar Behemoth gets +1/+1 until end of turn.', 'Target creature gets +3/+3 until end of turn.', 'Target creature gets +4/+4 until end of turn.', 'Target creature gets +7/+7 until end of turn.', 'Target creature gets +X/+0 until end of turn.', 'Target opponent reveals their hand. You choose a card from it. That player discards that card.', 'Target player discards a card for each Swamp you control.', 'Target player discards two cards.', 'Target player draws two cards.', 'Target player gains X life.', 'Target player loses 4 life and you gain 4 life.', "This spell can't be countered.\\nDestroy all artifacts, creatures, and lands. They can't be regenerated.", "Tidal Kraken can't be blocked.", 'Tremor deals 1 damage to each creature without flying.', 'Untap all creatures that attacked this turn. After this main phase, there is an additional combat phase followed by an additional main phase.', "Up to three target creatures can't block this turn.", 'Urborg Volcano enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {B} or {R}.', 'Vicious Hunger deals 2 damage to target creature and you gain 2 life.', 'Vigilance', 'Volcanic Hammer deals 3 damage to any target.', "Wall creatures can attack as though they didn't have defender.", 'When Death Pit Offering enters the battlefield, sacrifice all creatures you control.\\nCreatures you control get +2/+2.', 'When Elvish Pioneer enters the battlefield, you may put a basic land card from your hand onto the battlefield tapped.', 'When Gravedigger enters the battlefield, you may return target creature card from your graveyard to your hand.', 'When Hunted Wumpus enters the battlefield, each other player may put a creature card from their hand onto the battlefield.', 'When Maggot Carrier enters the battlefield, each player loses 1 life.', 'When Merchant of Secrets enters the battlefield, draw a card.', 'When Primeval Force enters the battlefield, sacrifice it unless you sacrifice three Forests.', 'When Ravenous Rats enters the battlefield, target opponent discards a card.', 'When Rukh Egg dies, create a 4/4 red Bird creature token with flying at the beginning of the next end step.', 'When Serpent Warrior enters the battlefield, you lose 3 life.', 'When Staunch Defenders enters the battlefield, you gain 4 life.', 'When Venerable Monk enters the battlefield, you gain 2 life.', 'When Wood Elves enters the battlefield, search your library for a Forest card, put that card onto the battlefield, then shuffle.', "When Wrath of Marit Lage enters the battlefield, tap all red creatures.\\nRed creatures don't untap during their controllers' untap steps.", 'When you control no other creatures, sacrifice Emperor Crocodile.', 'Whenever City of Brass becomes tapped, it deals 1 damage to you.\\n{T}: Add one mana of any color.', 'Whenever Deathgazer blocks or becomes blocked by a nonblack creature, destroy that creature at end of combat.', 'Whenever Elite Javelineer blocks, it deals 1 damage to target attacking creature.', 'Whenever Fungusaur is dealt damage, put a +1/+1 counter on it.', 'Whenever Giant Badger blocks, it gets +2/+2 until end of turn.', 'Whenever Lesser Gargadon attacks or blocks, sacrifice a land.', 'Whenever Seasoned Marshal attacks, you may tap target creature.', 'Whenever a Forest is tapped for mana, its controller adds an additional {G}.', "Whenever a creature becomes the target of a spell or ability, return that creature to its owner's hand. (It won't be affected by the spell or ability.)", "Whenever a creature dies, that creature's controller may draw a card.", "Whenever a creature is dealt damage, destroy it. It can't be regenerated.", 'Whenever a creature you control deals combat damage to a player, that player discards a card.', 'Whenever a creature you control deals combat damage to an opponent, you may draw a card.', 'Whenever a creature you control deals combat damage, you gain that much life.', 'Whenever a creature you control dies, each other player sacrifices a creature.', "Whenever a land is put into a graveyard from the battlefield, Dingus Egg deals 2 damage to that land's controller.", "Whenever a permanent is returned to a player's hand, that player discards a card.", 'Whenever a player casts a black spell, you may pay {1}. If you do, you gain 1 life.', 'Whenever a player casts a blue spell, you may pay {1}. If you do, you gain 1 life.', 'Whenever a player casts a green spell, you may pay {1}. If you do, you gain 1 life.', 'Whenever a player casts a red spell, you may pay {1}. If you do, you gain 1 life.', 'Whenever a player casts a white spell, you may pay {1}. If you do, you gain 1 life.', 'Whenever a spell or ability an opponent controls causes a land to be put into your graveyard from the battlefield, return that card to the battlefield.', 'Whenever an opponent casts a spell, Mogg Sentry gets +2/+2 until end of turn.', 'Whenever an opponent discards a card, Megrim deals 2 damage to that player.', 'Whenever an opponent draws a card, Underworld Dreams deals 1 damage to that player.', 'Whenever an opponent taps a Mountain for mana, you may gain 1 life.', 'Whenever you cast an enchantment spell, you may draw a card.', 'Yavimaya Enchantress gets +1/+1 for each enchantment on the battlefield.', "You and target opponent each flip a coin. Mana Clash deals 1 damage to each player whose coin comes up tails. Repeat this process until both players' coins come up heads on the same flip.", 'You draw three cards and you lose 3 life.', 'You gain 2 life for each creature you control.', 'You gain 3 life for each creature attacking you.', 'You gain 4 life.', 'You have no maximum hand size.', "You have shroud. (You can't be the target of spells or abilities.)", "You may have Lone Wolf assign its combat damage as though it weren't blocked.", "You may have Rhox assign its combat damage as though it weren't blocked.\\n{2}{G}: Regenerate Rhox. (The next time this creature would be destroyed this turn, it isn't. Instead tap it, remove all damage from it, and remove it from combat.)", "You may have Thorn Elemental assign its combat damage as though it weren't blocked.", 'You may tap or untap target artifact, creature, or land.', 'Your opponents play with their hands revealed.', "{1}: Return target land you control to its owner's hand.\\n{1}, Discard a land card: Draw a card.", '{1}: The next time a black source of your choice would deal damage to you this turn, prevent that damage.', '{1}: The next time a blue source of your choice would deal damage to you this turn, prevent that damage.', '{1}: The next time a green source of your choice would deal damage to you this turn, prevent that damage.', '{1}: The next time a red source of your choice would deal damage to you this turn, prevent that damage.', '{1}: The next time a white source of your choice would deal damage to you this turn, prevent that damage.', '{2}, {T}: Target creature gains flying until end of turn.', '{2}, {T}: Target player mills two cards.', "{2}{G}{G}: Reveal the top card of your library. If it's a creature card, put it onto the battlefield. Otherwise, put it into your graveyard.", '{2}{U}{U}: Draw a card.', '{3}, {T}: Rod of Ruin deals 1 damage to any target.', '{3}, {T}: Target player chooses a card name, then reveals the top card of their library. If that card has the chosen name, that player puts it into their hand. Otherwise, they put it into their graveyard and Vexing Arcanix deals 2 damage to them.', '{3}, {T}: Target player discards a card. Activate only during your turn.', '{3}: Patagia Golem gains flying until end of turn.', '{4}, {T}, Sacrifice a creature: Fodder Cannon deals 4 damage to target creature.', '{4}, {T}: Draw a card.', '{5}, {T}: Return target enchantment card from your graveyard to your hand.', '{6}, {T}: Search your library for a card, put that card into your hand, then shuffle.', "{8}, {T}: Aladdin's Ring deals 4 damage to any target.", '{B}, Sacrifice a creature: Target opponent reveals their hand. You choose a card from it. That player discards that card. Activate only as a sorcery.', '{B}: Looming Shade gets +1/+1 until end of turn.', '{B}: Primeval Shambler gets +1/+1 until end of turn.', "{B}: Regenerate Drudge Skeletons. (The next time this creature would be destroyed this turn, it isn't. Instead tap it, remove all damage from it, and remove it from combat.)", "{B}{B}, Pay half your life, rounded up: Destroy target nonblack creature. It can't be regenerated.", '{B}{B}, {T}: Destroy target green creature.', '{B}{B}, {T}: Destroy target white creature.', '{G}, Sacrifice a Forest: Foratog gets +2/+2 until end of turn.', '{G}, {T}, Sacrifice Elvish Lyrist: Destroy target enchantment.', '{G}, {T}, Sacrifice Elvish Scrapper: Destroy target artifact.', '{G}, {T}: Target creature gets +2/+2 until end of turn.', '{G}, {T}: You may put a creature card from your hand onto the battlefield.', '{G}: Regenerate Horned Troll.', '{R}, {T}: Anaba Shaman deals 1 damage to any target.', '{R}: Ridgeline Rager gets +1/+0 until end of turn.', '{T}, Sacrifice Daring Apprentice: Counter target spell.', '{T}, Sacrifice Phyrexian Plaguelord: Target creature gets -4/-4 until end of turn.\\nSacrifice a creature: Target creature gets -1/-1 until end of turn.', "{T}, Sacrifice a creature: Bloodshot Cyclops deals damage equal to the sacrificed creature's power to any target.", '{T}, Sacrifice an artifact: Draw a card.', "{T}: Add {C}. If you control an Urza's Mine and an Urza's Power-Plant, add {C}{C}{C} instead.", "{T}: Add {C}. If you control an Urza's Mine and an Urza's Tower, add {C}{C} instead.", "{T}: Add {C}. If you control an Urza's Power-Plant and an Urza's Tower, add {C}{C} instead.", '{T}: Add {G}{G}.', "{T}: All damage that would be dealt to target creature this turn by a source of your choice is dealt to Oracle's Attendants instead.", '{T}: Crossbow Infantry deals 1 damage to target attacking or blocking creature.', '{T}: Destroy target Wall.', '{T}: Destroy target creature with power 4 or greater.', '{T}: Destroy target tapped creature.', '{T}: Draw a card.', '{T}: Elite Archers deals 3 damage to target attacking or blocking creature.', "{T}: Look at the top three cards of target player's library.", '{T}: Orcish Artillery deals 2 damage to any target and 3 damage to you.', '{T}: Prevent the next 1 damage that would be dealt to any target this turn.', '{T}: Prevent the next 4 damage that would be dealt to any target this turn.', '{T}: Target permanent becomes the color of your choice until end of turn.', '{U}, {T}: You may tap or untap target creature.', "{U}{U}{U}, {T}: Return target permanent to its owner's hand.", '{W}, {T}: Tap target creature.', '{W}: Honor Guard gets +0/+1 until end of turn.', '{W}{W}: Target attacking creature gets -1/-0 until end of turn.']
flavor: ['"A flash of the lightning, a break of the wave,\\nHe passes from life to his rest in the grave."\\n—William Knox, "Mortality"', '"A good deal of tyranny goes by the name of protection."\\n—Crystal Eastman, "Equality or Protection"', '"A good lamp will light your way. A good ring will clear it."\\n—Nervan, royal jeweler', '"A stick is your friend. A pointed stick is your good friend. An army of pointed sticks is your best friend."\\n—Onean sergeant', '"Ach! Hans, run! It\'s the lhurgoyf!"\\n—Saffi Eriksdotter, last words', '"Any fool who would die for honor is better off dead."\\n—Cabal Patriarch', '"Be as fast as lightning, and you will be just as deadly."\\n—Combat trainer', '"Before my eyes was a horrible monster, worthy to figure in the legends of the marvellous. . . . Its eight arms, or rather feet, fixed to its head . . . were twice as long as its body, and were twisted like the furies\' hair."\\n—Jules Verne, *Twenty Thousand Leagues under the Sea*, trans. Lewis', '"Believe in the ideal, not the idol."\\n—Serra', '"Beware lest you lose the substance by grasping at the shadow."\\n—Aesop, *Fables*, trans. Jacobs', '"But high she shoots through air and light,\\nAbove all low delay,\\nWhere nothing earthly bounds her flight,\\nNor shadow dims her way."\\n—Thomas Moore, "Oh that I had Wings"', '"Catch!"', '"Cowards die many times before their deaths;\\nThe valiant never taste of death but once."\\n—William Shakespeare, *Julius Caesar*', '"Cry to the sun and watch as even your tears forsake you."\\n—Acolyte of Marit Lage', '"Destruction is the work of an afternoon. Creation is the work of a lifetime."', '"Expect nothing but scorn, flattery, and lies. And never turn your back on him."\\n—Northern paladin', '"For what are leaves but countless blades\\nTo fight a countless foe on high."\\n—Elvish hymn', '"From the snowy slopes of Kaelor,\\nTo the canyons of Bandu,\\nWe drink and fight and feast and die\\nAs we were born to do."\\n—Balduvian tavern song', '"Getting people to do what you want is merely a matter of telling them what they want to hear."', '"Graceful? Yes. Beautiful? Absolutely. Harmless? Definitely not."\\n—Fyndhorn elder', '"Guess where I\'m gonna plant this!"', '"Ha, banishment? Be merciful, say \'death,\'\\nFor exile hath more terror in his look,\\nMuch more than death."\\n—William Shakespeare, *Romeo and Juliet*', '"He can split a marshfly in two from halfway across the range."\\n—Onean sergeant', '"Human tenderness is simply weakness in a pretty package."', '"Hup, two, three, four,\\nDunno how to count no more."\\n—Mogg march', '"I am bound to all my children. I share in their joys, I rage at their injuries."', '"I can\'t think with all that screaming."', '"I confer with Death itself. What could you possibly do to injure me?"', '"I don\'t like to think of myself as a pirate. I\'m more like a stimulator of the local economy."', '"I heard their eerie howling, the wolves calling their kindred across the frozen plains."\\n—Onean scout', '"I love lightning! It\'s my best invention since the rock."\\n—Toggo, goblin weaponsmith', '"I wouldn\'t stand in front of that wurm, son. \'Course, I wouldn\'t stand behind it neither. In fact, standing anywhere near that wurm\'s not much of a plan. Running, now *that\'s* a plan!"\\n—Wandering mage', '"I\'ve seen my master do this a hundred times. How hard can it be?"', '"In some cultures, elephants are ridden by those in power. I don\'t think a mere elephant would even be noticed in Keld."\\n—Onean sergeant', '"In the drowsy dark cave of the mind, dreams build their nest with fragments dropped from day\'s caravan."\\n—Rabindranath Tagore', '"It is better to take what does not belong to you than to let it lie around neglected."\\n—Mark Twain, *More Maxims of Mark*', '"It is not a choice I make, to have this guard. It is the choice of my people, and my duty to them."\\n—Oracle *en*-Vec', '"It is useful to be able to speak to the trees. But it is truly wondrous to be able to listen to them."', '"Kill them all and feed them to the new recruits."\\n—Crovax, ascendant evincar', '"Knowledge demands sacrifice."', '"Knowledge is power."\\n—Sir Francis Bacon, *Meditationes Sacrae*', '"Let me redeem my brothers both from death."\\n—William Shakespeare, *Titus Andronicus*', '"Let\'s go over this one more time. . . ."', '"Let\'s see . . . Mercadia, mercenary, merfolk . . . you know, I really need a better filing system."', '"Marit Lage lies frozen in a glacier\'s heart. Still her dreams take form in our world, stealing the heat from our souls."\\n—Halvor Arenson, Kjeldoran priest', '"Mercy? Mercy is for the playground, not the battleground."', '"Most people can\'t build decent weapons out of stone or steel. Trust the elves to do it with only mud and vines."\\n—Gerrard of the *Weatherlight*', '"Neither could I forget what I had read of these pits—that the *sudden* extinction of life formed no part of their most horrible plan."\\n—Edgar Allan Poe,\\n"The Pit and the Pendulum"', '"Of all the tyrannies on humane kind\\nThe worst is that which persecutes the mind."\\n—John Dryden,\\n"The Hind and the Panther"', '"Of course she\'s at the head of her class. All of her classmates have disappeared."\\n—Tolarian renegade', '"Of course you should fight fire with fire. You should fight *everything* with fire."\\n—Jaya Ballard, task mage', '"One day we shall walk where once was water."\\n—Eladamri, Lord of Leaves', '"One touch of nature makes the whole world kin."\\n—William Shakespeare,\\n*Troilus and Cressida*', '"Over the silver mountains,\\nWhere spring the nectar fountains,\\nThere will I kiss\\nThe bowl of bliss;\\nAnd drink my everlasting fill. . . ."\\n—Sir Walter Raleigh, "The Pilgrimage"', '"Pound the steel until it fits. Doesn\'t work? Bash to bits."\\n—Dwarven forging song', '"Precision is frequently more valuable than force."', '"Rats, rats, rats! Hundreds, thousands, millions of them, and every one a life."\\n—Bram Stoker, *Dracula*', '"Returne from whence ye came. . . ."\\n—Edmund Spenser, *The Faerie Queene*', '"Secrets? What secrets?"', '"So much for that bright idea!"', '"So they want to kill my men? Well two can play at that game."\\n—General Khurzog', '"Some believe sandstalkers to be illusions; those with scars know better."\\n—*Zhalfirin Guide to the Desert*', '"Some have said there is no subtlety to destruction. You know what? They\'re dead."\\n—Jaya Ballard, task mage', '"The Eye altering alters all."\\n—William Blake, "The Mental Traveller"', '"The beasts of the wild are my senses. It is through their eyes that all knowledge shall come to me."', '"The bonds of loyalty can tie one to the grave."\\n—Crovax, ascendant evincar', '"The day of Spirits; my soul\'s calm retreat / Which none disturb!"\\n—Henry Vaughan, "The Night"', '"The dead make good soldiers. They can\'t disobey orders, they never surrender, and they don\'t stop fighting when a random body part falls off."\\n—Nevinyrral, *Necromancer\'s Handbook*', '"The enemy has been destroyed, sir. So have the forest, the city, your palace, your dog . . ."\\n—Keldon soldier', '"The final stage of the illness: delirium, convulsions, and death."\\n—Phyrexian progress notes', '"The first birth celebrates life. The second birth mocks it."\\n—Mystic elder', '"The first wind of ascension is Forger, burning away impurity."\\n—*Keld Triumphant*', '"The horror! The horror!"\\n—Joseph Conrad, *Heart of Darkness*', '"The love of nature . . . is a furious, burning, physical greed. . . ."\\n—Mary Webb, *The House in Dormer Forest*', '"The mortal world is a grove of sweet fruit, and I am ready to harvest it."\\n—Fallen angel', '"The peasants labor for my profit. I approve."', '"The second wind of ascension is Reaver, slaying the unworthy."\\n—*Keld Triumphant*', '"The smell of roasted flesh hung over the valley for hours."\\n—Onean sergeant', '"The spirit of the devout is easily crushed by the loss of hope."\\n—Fallen angel', '"The stories tell of a distant time when machines overran the forests, destroying everything that lived. That time will not come again."', '"The treasure in my mind is greater than any worldly glory."', '"Their eyes will shrivel and blacken before faith\'s true light."', '"There is no worse enemy. His passion for death doesn\'t just border on insanity, it wallows in it."\\n—Southern paladin', '"There\'s never been a dwarven smith who could match the marvels that Gaea herself forges."\\n—Elvish champion', '"They groaned, they stirred, they all uprose,\\nNor spake, nor moved their eyes;\\nIt had been strange, even in a dream,\\nTo have seen those dead men rise."\\n—Samuel Taylor Coleridge,\\n"The Rime of the Ancient Mariner"', '"Those who fear the darkness have never seen what the light can do."\\n—Selenia, dark angel', '"To empty your mind is to fill your grave."\\n—Lat-Nam teaching', '"Training? Seeing my crops burnt to cinders was all the \'training\' I needed."', '"True power is controlling not only the hearts of your subjects, but their minds as well."', '"Trust me—the walls have more than just ears."\\n—Orcish spy', '"We are the hands of the great trees, reaching out to ensnare what threatens their branches."\\n—Elvish hunter', '"We do not suddenly fall on death, but advance towards it by slight degrees; we die every day."\\n—Seneca, *Epistles*, trans. Gummere', '"We must all hang together, or assuredly we shall all hang separately."\\n—Benjamin Franklin', '"We three, though of separate ancestry, join in brotherhood. . . . We dare not hope to be together always but hereby vow to die the selfsame day."\\n—Peach Garden Oath', '"Wealth means power; the power to subdue, to crush, to exploit, the power to enslave, to outrage, to degrade."\\n—Emma Goldman, "Anarchism"', '"What\'s got two arms, one wing, and no brains?"\\n—Ghitu riddle', '"When every reef is bared and every wave is dust—only then shall I rest."', '"When the air burns, only death breathes deep."\\n—Bogardan mage', '"When the forest wants something, no mortal mind can resist her."\\n—Maro', '"Who says lightning never strikes twice?"\\n—Storm shaman', '"Why build a bridge that needs to be guarded?"\\n—Elvish champion', '"Why do we pray to the Ancestor? Because She listens."\\n—Mystic elder', '"Why do you weep for the dead? I rejoice, for they have died for me."', '"Why should death always have the last word?"\\n—Llanowar druid', '"Words—so innocent and powerless are they, as standing in a dictionary; how potent for good and evil they become to one who knows how to combine them!"\\n—Nathaniel Hawthorne', '"You idiot! Never let the spies mingle with the orcish regulars after completing a mission. Now we\'ll never get them to fight!"\\n—General Khurzog', '"You know that secret? The one that wakes you up at night in a cold sweat? The one you think no one else in the world knows? Well, guess what."', '"You wouldn\'t like me when I\'m angry."', 'A beacon in the night, a dream in the fog.', 'A bored wizard once created a vizzerdrix out of a bunny and a piranha. He never made *that* mistake again.', 'A drop of humanity for a sea of power.', 'A fool knows no fear. A hero shows no fear.', 'A full coffin is like a full coffer—both are attractive to thieves.', 'A hiss before dying.', 'A skilled decoy can throw your enemies off your trail. A master decoy can survive to do it again.', 'A song of life soars over fields of blood.', 'A wall built from the bodies of the enemy will never lack building material in times of war.', 'A wolf without a pack is either a survivor or a brute.', "After the battle, an eerie silence gripped the forest. The losers' remains were lightly dusted with green.", 'After their first encounter, the goblins named him Chuck.', 'Age wears the flesh but galvanizes the soul.', 'Anyone can get around a cyclops, but few can stand in its way.', 'Armodons are trained to step on things. Enemy things.', 'As long as the dryads are a part of the forest, the forest is a part of the army.', "Bent on a quest for blood, a giant can storm through a fort's wall as if it were nothing more than a picket fence.", 'Bitter as wormwood, sweet as mulled wine.', 'Blessed by a thousand prayers.', 'Called "stonefeathers" by many lowlanders, rukhs are thought to descend from a phoenix that sacrificed its flame for a body of stone.', 'Deep in the heart of Urborg lie massive volcanoes whose thick black smoke covers the land with perpetual darkness.', 'Disturb a sleeping badger and the snapping of your bones will awaken the countryside.', "Don't try to outrun one of Dominaria's grizzlies; it'll catch you, knock you down, and eat you. Of course, you could run up a tree. In that case you'll get a nice view before it knocks the tree down and eats you.", 'Dry grass is tinder before the spark.', 'Each pluck of the strings breaks the hold of the unnatural on the world.', 'Each victory adds a new verse.', 'Earth arms itself with fire.', 'Even an enemy is a valuable resource.', 'Even the brave are scared by a lion three times: first by its tracks, again by its roar, and one last time face to face.\\n—Somali proverb', "Even what is lost beyond recall returns when coaxed by a dryad's hand.", 'Every branch a crossroads, every vine a swift steed.', 'Fighting for the right reason is itself a source of strength.', 'Fire finds its form in the heat of the forge.', 'Fire never dies alone.', 'Five hundred years to grow—barely a minute to eat.', 'Foolishly, Najib retreated to his castle at El-Abar; the next morning he was dead. In just one night, the dwarven forces had reduced the mighty walls to mere rubble.', 'For the first time in his life, Grakk felt a little warm and fuzzy inside.', 'Forged by a thousand flames.', "From Gaea grew the world, and the world was silent. From Gaea grew the world's elves, and the world was silent no more.\\n—Elvish teaching", 'From a whisper to a roar, the call is heard by all and refused by none.', 'Get in touch with your inner monster.', 'Greed and gluttony led him to death. Now they are his greatest assets.', 'He raged at the world, at his family, at his life. But mostly he just raged.', "He's smart for a goblin. He can do *two* things: hit *and* run.", 'Healers ultimately acquire the divine gifts of spiritual and physical wholeness. The most devout are also granted the ability to pass physical wholeness on to others.', 'Heavy light flooded across the landscape, cloaking everything in deep crimson.', "Her heart holds the pain of every soldier she's ever healed.", "Her roots connect her to the forest's wishes.", "His mind, like his body, is made up of the swamp's flotsam.", 'If only every message were as perfect as its bearer.', 'In Mercadia City, loyalties extend only as far as your purse can stretch.', 'In the warrior kingdom of Keld, the cats used in the hunt are prized for their tracking sense and ability to climb walls.', "It can pass through solid matter—but that doesn't mean it's harmless.", 'It despises humans and squirrels and beasts and dwarves and cephalids . . . well, it despises just about everything.', 'It dodges waves of water to prepare for waves of magic.', 'It does not wear a crown or sit on a throne of gold, but those who have witnessed its power hail it nonetheless.', "It doesn't like having visitors . . . unless it's having them for lunch.", "It doesn't point north. It points home.", "It doesn't think. It doesn't feel.\\nIt doesn't laugh or cry.\\nAll it does from dusk till dawn\\nIs make the soldiers die.\\n—Onean children's rhyme", "It has germinated in the earth for thousands of years. Finally it wakes to the battle's call.", 'It keeps the upper reaches of the forest free of every menace . . . except for the spider itself.', "It's easy to believe the monster is a myth—until you feel three hundred thousand pounds of myth crashing down on your ship.", 'Its diet consists of fruits, plants, small woodland animals, large woodland animals, woodlands, fruit groves, fruit farmers, and small cities.', 'Its eye the glaring sun, its cry the keening wind.', 'Its wings were only designed to be ornamental, but it learned to use them on its own.', 'Jamuraan farmers fear three things above all else: droughts, floods, and hornclaws.', 'Just as each added feather steadies the wing, so does the flock grow stronger with each new member.', 'Just one can feed a dozen people for a month.', 'Just try taking *this* bull by the horns.', "Keep watch only for the giants and you'll be eaten by the ants.", 'Knights fight for honor and mercenaries fight for gold. The militia fights for hearth and home.', 'Knowledge knows no bounds.', 'Lat-Nam wizards trade knowledge on scrolls made of magic so they can better guard against thieves and spies.', 'Legend has it that the mine howls out the last words of those who died inside.', 'Legend has it that the world was hatched from a dingus egg.', 'Life is eternal. A lifetime is ephemeral.', "Made from its wearer's hopes, the mask ensures that those hopes will be fulfilled.", 'Madness and genius are separated only by degrees of success.', 'Master the sky and you rule everything beneath it.\\n—Metathran saying', 'Memories cut from the mind can cut right back.', 'Mold crept over the walls and into every crevice until the gleaming white stone strained and burst.', 'More than one mage has been driven insane by the sound of the millstone relentlessly grinding away.', 'Most people know better. Goblins only know bigger.', 'Most soldiers think of the sword as a weapon. In the hands of Zho monks, swords are also the strongest of shields.', 'Nature grows solutions to her problems.', 'Nature twists knots stronger than any rope.', 'No fear. No sense. And soon, no lunch.', 'No one in Aphetto answers a knock at the door after sundown.', 'No one knows whether they were named for the disease they carry or for the speed at which they multiply.', 'No two see the same Maro.', 'Nothing is sacred to the rats. Everything is simply another meal.', 'Of royal blood among the spirits of the air, the Mahamoti djinn rides on the wings of the winds. As dangerous in the gambling hall as he is in battle, he is a master of trickery and misdirection.', 'Ogres learn how to smash stuff even before they learn how to walk.', 'On darkness feeding, in nightmares breeding.', 'One footstep among many is silent. One footstep alone is deafening.', 'Only death breeds in stagnant water.\\n—Urborg saying', 'Only the hardiest explorers survive to eat the fruit.', 'Only the most ravenous soul feeds on the health of the weak.', 'Opportunity makes the thief.\\n—Roman proverb', 'Other birds collect twigs for their nests. Magpies steal jewels for theirs.', 'Polished by a thousand waves.', "Pray that it doesn't seek the safety of your lungs.", 'Rain from this storm leaves you pinned to the ground like an insect.', 'Rather than sheltering her young, the female fungusaur often injures her own offspring, thereby ensuring their rapid growth.', 'Scholars in their ivory towers call them "sharks of the sky." Scholars on the road don\'t call them at all.', 'Sharper than wind, lighter than air.', 'She reads the battlefield like a map, always seeking the shortest route to victory.', 'Some fishers like to eat eels, and some eels like to eat fishers.', 'Some say they are the weapons of heroes fallen in battle, eager for one last chance at glory.', 'Some warriors walk the earth. Others are born of it.', 'Sometimes everyone decides to go for help at the same time.', 'Sometimes the wings of fallen dragons refuse to give up the sky.', 'Step 1: Find your cousin. Step 2: Get your cousin in the cannon. Step 3: Find another cousin.', 'Storm crow descending, winter unending. Storm crow departing, summer is starting.', 'Strengthened by a thousand limbs.', 'Such power grows the body as it shrinks the soul.', "Sword hilts jut from some trolls' bodies where wounds healed so fast that the weapons were trapped inside.", 'Tainted by a thousand fears.', 'The College of Lat-Nam is often forced to expel students whose experiments grow too risky or too cruel.', 'The best ideas often come from the worst minds.', 'The bodies of its victims are the only tracks it leaves.', 'The deep sleep of winter is not always restful.', 'The earth cannot hold that which magic commands.', 'The elfhames are the closest thing to "civilization" the elves allow themselves.', 'The elves had the edge in guile, skill, and valor. But in the end, only sheer numbers mattered.', "The elves' battle cries cut paths through the Æther, guiding those who would stand in Gaea's defense.", 'The fatal flaw in every plan is the assumption that you know more than your enemy.', 'The furnace awaits the next master who would stoke the fires of apocalypse.', "The future isn't sacred, but its speaker is.", 'The golden rule of revenge: Do unto others what they tried to do unto you.', 'The ground itself lends its strength to these walls of living stone, which possess the stability of ancient mountains. These mighty bulwarks thwart ground-based troops, providing welcome relief for weary warriors who defend the land.', 'The hardest part of his training is learning not to eat the boar.', 'The heavier the load, the harder it works.', 'The key to winning any fight is simply staying alive.', "The king of Yavimaya's waters pays constant attention to his subjects . . . and thrives on their adulation.", 'The land will never betray those who gave their lives for it.', 'The less you have, the harder you fight for it.', 'The most terrifying thing about the craw wurm is probably the horrible crashing sound it makes as it speeds through the forest. This noise is so loud it echoes through the trees and seems to come from all directions at once.', 'The rod is a relic from ancient times . . . cruel, vicious, mean-spirited times.', 'The same spears that catch their food today will defend their homes tomorrow.', 'The song of the forest is in perfect harmony. If a single note is out of place, the elves will find its source.', 'The sun breaks, the beasts stir, and the forest awakens to stand against its enemies.', 'The thunder of its hooves beats dreams into despair.', "The turning of the tide always begins with one soldier's decision to head back into the fray.", 'The undisputed master of the mountains of Shiv.', 'The wise, the righteous, the mighty—the merchant feeds them all.', 'These devices have been known to pull entire worlds through the Æther.', 'They feed on the living to stay undead.', 'They fletch their arrows with the feathers of angels.', 'Think of it as a butcher knife with wings.', 'Though lifeless, the skull still possessed a strange power over the flow of magic.', "Though those who study are as many as the hairs on an ox, those who succeed are as rare as unicorns' horns.\\n—Chinese proverb", 'To a dryad, every tree in the forest is both a doorway and a window.', 'To a sabretooth, all men are mice.', 'To be king, Numsgil did in Blog, who did in Unkful, who did in Viddle, who did in Loll, who did in Alrok. . . .', 'To gaze under its hood is to invite death.', "To merfolk, pirates are a nuisance. To pirates, merfolk are a threat. To the kraken, they're both appetizers.", 'To outrace the griffin\\n—Kipamu expression meaning "to do the impossible"', "To renew the land, plow the land.\\nTo destroy the land, do nothing.\\n—Druids' saying", 'To scrape out a living in Aphetto, wizards are reduced to selling rumors, lies, forgeries, or—if they get desperate enough—the truth.', "Toren had stepped on a lot of bugs during his life, so he couldn't help feeling embarrassed when a bug stepped on him.", 'Tortured with magic by their masters, the moggs are enflamed by the smell of sorcery.', 'Trained in the arts of stealth, royal assassins choose their victims carefully, relying on timing and precision rather than brute force.', 'Unanswered prayers are themselves answers.\\n—Nantuko teaching', 'Urza protected his body well, but neglected his soul.', "Verick held his breath. Breathing wouldn't reveal his position, but it would force him to smell the goblins.", 'War is a conflict that determines not who is right—but who is left.', 'Watching the spider\'s web\\n—Llanowar expression meaning "focusing on the wrong thing"', 'What it lacks in backbone, it makes up for in cruelty.', 'What wizards fear most is losing their minds.', 'When no falcons fly, beware the sky.\\n—Femeref aphorism', 'When she flies above the good, they consider themselves blessed. When she flies above the wicked, they consider themselves dead.', 'When you get into the swamp, the swamp gets into you.', 'Where air meets water, fish meets talon.', 'Where do you run when the earth becomes your enemy?', 'Which hurts more: a sword in the gut or a dagger in the back?', 'Which is more unsettling: the roar of battle or the silence that follows?', 'While armies battled across Jamuraa, beasts stalked the high places looking for victims.', "Within each device is a spark of its creator's soul. Within each sage is a lamp that awaits that spark.", 'Woven from strands of griffin mane and pegasus tail.', 'You are who you eat.', 'Your entire life passes before its eyes.']
artist: ['Adam Rex', 'Adrian Smith', 'Alan Pollack', 'Alan Rabinowitz', 'Alex Horley-Orlandelli', 'Andrew Goldhawk', 'Andrew Robinson', 'Anson Maddocks', 'Anthony S. Waters', 'Arnie Swekel', 'Ben Thompson', 'Berry', 'Bob Eggleton', 'Brian Despain', 'Brian Snõddy', 'Brom', 'Carl Critchlow', 'Chippy', 'Christopher Moeller', 'Christopher Rush', 'D. Alexander Gregory', 'D. J. Cleland-Hura', 'Dan Frazier', 'Dana Knutson', 'Daniel Gelon', 'Dany Orizio', 'Daren Bader', 'Darrell Riche', 'Dave Dorman', 'David Martin', 'Dermot Power', 'DiTerlizzi', 'Don Hazeltine', 'Donato Giancola', 'Edward P. Beard, Jr.', 'Eric Peterson', 'Franz Vohwinkel', 'Fred Fields', 'Gary Leach', 'Gary Ruddell', 'Glen Angus', 'Glen Angus & Arnie Swekel', 'Greg Hildebrandt', 'Greg Hildebrandt & Tim Hildebrandt', 'Greg Staples', 'Hannibal King', 'Heather Hudson', 'James Bernardin', 'Janine Johnston', 'Jason Alexander Behnke', 'Jeff Miracola', 'Jeremy Jarvis', 'Jerry Tiritilli', 'Jim Nelson', 'Joel Biske', 'John Avon', 'John Howe', 'John Matson', 'John Zeleznik', 'Junko Taguchi', 'Justin Sweet', 'Keith Parkinson', 'Kev Walker', 'Kevin Murphy', 'Larry Elmore', 'Lars Grant-West', 'Luca Zontini', 'Marc Fishman', 'Mark Brill', 'Mark Poole', 'Mark Romanoski', 'Mark Tedin', 'Mark Zug', 'Massimilano Frezzato', 'Matt Cavotta', 'Matt Thompson', 'Matthew D. Wilson', 'Matthew Mitchell', 'Melissa A. Benson', 'Michael Koelsch', 'Michael Sutfin', 'Mike Ploog', 'Monte Michael Moore', 'Paolo Parente', 'Patrick Faricy', 'Pete Venters', 'Peter Bollinger', 'Puddnhead', 'Qiao Dafu', 'Randy Gallegos', 'Rebecca Guay', 'Richard Sardinha', 'Richard Thomas', 'Rick Farrell', 'Rob Alexander', 'Robert Bliss', 'Roger Raupp', 'Ron Spears', 'Ron Spencer', 'Ron Walotsky', 'Sam Wood', 'Scott Bailey', 'Scott M. Fischer', 'Stephen Daniele', 'Steve Luke', 'Steve White', 'Stuart Griffin', 'Terese Nielsen', 'Thomas M. Baxa', 'Tim Hildebrandt', 'Todd Lockwood', 'Tom Kyffin', 'Tom Wänerstrand', 'Tony Szczudlo', 'Tristan Elwell', 'Una Fricker', 'Wayne England', 'rk post']
